,"html_url":"https://github.com/finnbuhse","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finnbuhse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finnbuhse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finnbuhse/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finnbuhse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finnbuhse/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finnbuhse/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finnbuhse/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finnbuhse/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/finnbuhse/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-25T12:05:11Z","updated_at":"2023-08-25T12:05:11Z","body":"I think I could be experiencing this same issue. I am using an FBX model originally from Mixamo exported from Blender. I noticed in one of my animations the character's leg was 'snapping' to an incorrect transform for a split second. I thought it was something to do with the interpolation but after playing through the animation frame by frame I found it was the animation data itself. And seemingly the issue only occurs with rotations. I have tried ensuring that the W component within each quaternion is > 0.0 as suggested in this post: 'https://gamedev.stackexchange.com/questions/27547/frame-interpolation-issues-for-skeletal-animation'. But no luck. Here are what my animation frames look like:\r\nFirst frame (before):\r\n![Screenshot (260)](https://github.com/assimp/assimp/assets/50274957/e9a4e151-c210-46d3-829e-9c4f2b0a6261)\r\nSecond frame (incorrect / inverted rotation):\r\n![Screenshot (261)](https://github.com/assimp/assimp/assets/50274957/4413626d-57fd-43d4-b870-f9d637d5c181)\r\nThird frame (after)\r\n![Screenshot (262)](https://github.com/assimp/assimp/assets/50274957/6bead969-252e-4e2f-a02e-b366a74f35a2)\r\n\r\nI find it very bizarre that the rest 